# Values that MUST be identical across backend/ and ai-injury-assistant/.
#
# Copy this file to .env.shared (git-ignored) and fill it in. Each app loads
# its own .env first and this file second, so an app-specific file always wins
# -- that is what keeps backend/.env.test authoritative when running tests.
#
# Only put a variable here if two apps genuinely have to agree on it. Anything
# used by a single app belongs in that app's own .env. In particular PORT does
# NOT belong here: backend/ uses 3001 and ai-injury-assistant/ uses 3002, and
# hosts such as Render inject PORT themselves.
#
# frontend/ deliberately does not read this file. Its NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# compiled into the browser bundle, so they stay in frontend/.env.local, well
# away from anything secret. ai-injury-extractor/ is an AWS Lambda and takes
# its environment from Terraform, not from a file.

# Signing secret for auth tokens. backend/ issues them; ai-injury-assistant/
# verifies them. If these two ever differ, every assistant request fails as
# "unauthenticated" with nothing in the logs explaining why.
JWT_SECRET=

# Both apps read the same database. backend/ owns the schema (including the
# DocumentChunk table the assistant writes vectors into); the assistant reads
# the user's real journal data and never migrates.
#
# Pointing the assistant at a different database is what made it answer from
# seeded records nobody had written.
DATABASE_URL=
